WEBVTT

00:11:59.452 --> 00:12:02.853
and it goes back 500 years.

00:12:03.244 --> 00:12:07.545
And it shows real GDP.

00:12:07.569 --> 00:12:08.735
In other words,

00:12:08.759 --> 00:12:11.609
the economic activity going back there.

00:12:11.633 --> 00:12:12.848
And there's a line.

00:12:12.872 --> 00:12:17.562
And you don't see these depressions,
as we're calling them,

00:12:17.586 --> 00:12:19.847
even on that line that barely wiggles.

00:12:19.871 --> 00:12:24.079
When you go into it
and you look at that piece,

00:12:24.103 --> 00:12:25.358
that's what it looks like.

00:12:25.382 --> 00:12:28.025
GDP falls 10 percent,
unemployment goes up,

00:12:28.049 --> 00:12:29.450
and it passes.

00:12:29.752 --> 00:12:34.560
And because the greatest force
is the force of adaptation